            0.164,
            0.358,
            0.885,
            0.455
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose the number of children is kept the same, but the number of units that are being shared is increased? What can you say about each child’s share now? Why? Discuss how your reasoning explains "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\textstyle { \\frac { 1 } { 5 } }   <   { \\frac { 2 } { 5 } }   , \\; { \\frac { 3 } { 7 } }   <   { \\frac { 4 } { 7 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 } \\; < \\; \\frac { 5 } { 8 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.471,
            0.884,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, decide in which of the two groups will each child get a larger share:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.525,
            0.768,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Group 1 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 3 glasses of sugarcane juice divided equally among 4 children."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
